            <div class="content-section">
                <div id="pgp-rise-tab1" class="content active">

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30 active" data-rel="tab-a-1">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">Is PGP Rise: General Management equivalent to other Executive MBA Programmes offered in
                                the country?</p>

                            <img  src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer" id="tab-a-1">The academic content and rigour of the Masters’ Union PGP Rise: General Management
                            are equivalent to other Executive MBA programmes. However, Indian regulations do not allow
                            independent institutions to grant a Master’s degree. After completion of the programme,
                            applicants will receive a certificate of completion of the Post Graduate Programme in
                            Management for Senior Professionals.</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-a-2">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">Can applicants continue to work full-time while pursuing the
                                programme?
                            </p>

                            <img  src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer" id="tab-a-2">Yes, applicants can continue their full-time job as they
                            pursue PGP Rise: General Management by Masters’ Union.</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-a-3">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">What happens when applicants are not in the residency?
                            </p>

                            <img  src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer" id="tab-a-3">Their studies will continue on the weekend in a hybrid model
                            where they can choose to attend in-person classes at our Gurgaon campus or join in
                            virtually.</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-a-4">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">What will be the batch size of the class?</p>

                            <img  src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer" id="tab-a-4">We will limit the batch size to a maximum of 60 students to
                            maximize individual attention from masters, and have an impactful teacher-student ratio.</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-a-5">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">What are the core emphasis areas of the Masters’ Union PGP Rise: General Management
                                curriculum?</p>

                            <img  src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <div id="tab-a-5" class="faqanswer">
                            <p>We offer India’s first programme with industry-focused coaching at its core. Students get
                                expert mentorship to define their career goals. They benefit from psychometric
                                assessments and industry-focused coaching, all tailored to meet the following needs of
                                mid-career professionals:</p>

                            <ul>
                                <li class="subText">Mid-career transition guidance</li>
                                <li class="subText">Enhancing your professional brand</li>
                                <li class="subText">Interview preparation strategy</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-a-6">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">How many days of leave will an applicant require to participate in the
                                immersive weeks?</p>

                            <img  src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer" id="tab-a-6">Applicants will require around 10 days of leave
                            throughout the year to participate in the campus immersion weeks, tech-trek, and leadership
                            retreat.</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-a-7">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">What is included in the cost of the programme?</p>

                            <img  src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>

                        <div id="tab-a-7" class="faqanswer">
                            <p>The programme fee for the PGP Rise: General Management by Masters’ Union will cover:</p>

                            <ul>
                                <li class="subText">Tuition fees for courses, workshops, retreats & events</li>
                                <li class="subText">All dining excursions organised by the PGP Rise: General Management team including
                                    breakfast, lunch, dinner, snacks</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-a-8">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">How much time should an applicant set aside for coursework on the
                                weekdays?</p>

                            <img  src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer" id="tab-a-8">We will try to keep any additional coursework on weekdays to a
                            bare minimum. However, the time taken to prepare for classes can vary according to the
                            subject and applicants’ expertise on the same. On average applicants can expect to spend
                            5-10 hours a week on weekdays. There will be additional material provided to the applicants
                            in the form of written content, videos or podcasts that they can choose to engage with at
                            their convenience.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-a-9">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading"> Is the PGP Rise: General Management model as valuable as a full-time residential PGP?</p>

                            <img  src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer" id="tab-a-9">While the programme design differs from that of a full-time
                            PGP, the curriculum and structure is equivalent to that of any recognized executive MBA
                            globally. The structure is designed to be flexible to accommodate the busy schedules of
                            working professionals and the content is tailored for those with considerable work
                            experience.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-a-10">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading"> What are the benefits of the 1-year format?</p>

                            <img  src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer" id="tab-a-10"> PGP Rise: General Management by Masters’ Union, with its unique 12-month
                            weekend format covers best-in-class practices in global executive management education
                            through an accelerated pedagogical approach. Designed to offer flexibility as a working
                            professional so applicants don’t have to leave their job to pursue the course, the 4 terms
                            will cover rigorous academic training in core areas. Applicants can choose to go deeper in
                            the industry of their choice through industry electives and find stellar opportunities to
                            network with like-minded individuals through the residency weeks, a tech-trek and leadership
                            retreat. The dynamic format of the programme will offer accelerated learning in the skills
                            of time management and prioritisation, and thus equips them with stellar decision-making
                            facilities, which is one of the most valued qualities of a business leader in today’s times.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                </div>

