                    </div> --}}
                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-c-4">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">Who are we looking for? </p>

                            <img  src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer font-16 font-grey13" id="tab-c-4">We are looking for a candidate who
                            exhibits strong leadership performance and potential, makes the best use of opportunities
                            available, and is motivated to create an impact.
                        </p>
                    </div>


                </div>
                <div id="pgp-rise-tab4" class="content">
                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-d-1">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">Do we need to write a GMAT, GRE, or CAT to enrol
                                in this programme?</p>

                            <img  src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer font-16 font-grey13" id="tab-d-1">No, this programme doesn’t require GMAT,
                            GRE, or CAT scores.</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-d-2">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">Can applicants get their profile evaluated?</p>

                            <img  src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer font-16 font-grey13" id="tab-d-2">Feel free to connect with the admissions
                            team and our counsellors to discuss fitment with the programme. Applicants are welcome to
                            send their CV to <a href="mailto:pgpriseadmissions@mastersunion.org" class="link-red"> 
                                pgpriseadmissions@mastersunion.org</a> and initiate a conversation with our counsellors
                            for the same.</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-d-3">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">Are all candidates interviewed?</p>

                            <img  src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer font-16 font-grey13" id="tab-d-3">Post the application process, the
                            shortlisted candidates are invited to an online interview with our admissions panel.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-d-4">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">If an application has been unsuccessful, may
                                they reapply in the next round?</p>

                            <img  src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer font-16 font-grey13" id="tab-d-4">No, they cannot reapply in the next round.
                            Unsuccessful applicants can reapply for the next intake, next year. Re-applicants are
                            requested to submit a new online application unless otherwise indicated.
                            Please exercise judgement in deciding if they have made any significant changes in their new
                            profile since their first application, that would make a significant difference to their
                            admissions chances. </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-d-5">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">How strict are the application deadlines?</p>

                            <img  src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer font-16 font-grey13" id="tab-d-5">Our deadlines are non-negotiable.
                            Applications must be completed and submitted by midnight (Indian Standard Time) to be
                            included in the ongoing round. A complete application includes the online form, all
                            supporting documents, references, essays, and payment of the application fees.</p>
                    </div>


                </div>
                <div id="pgp-rise-tab5" class="content">

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-e-1">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">How will applicants be graded for the course?
                            </p>

                            <img  src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer font-16 font-grey13" id="tab-e-1">All participants will be graded through a
                            combination of quizzes, exams, group assignments, class engagement, projects, simulations,
                            reflections, etc. The faculty will decide the specific grading matrix for each course.</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-e-2">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">Can applicants tailor their learning journey at
                                PGP Rise: General Management?
                            </p>

                            <img  src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer font-16 font-grey13" id="tab-e-2">We offer 16 electives, empowering students
                            to take charge of their time and construct a relevant programme that is aligned with their
                            interests and career goals. We have new-age, core, and industry concentrations so they can
                            choose to pursue a generalist path toward management or specialise in particular areas by
                            choosing industry concentrations. However, regardless of the path students decide to take
                            during their elective terms, everybody graduates with the same PGP Rise: General Management certificate with an
                            opportunity to choose industry concentrations.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-e-3">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">Are any of the rounds more or less competitive
                                than others?</p>

                            <img  src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer font-16 font-grey13" id="tab-e-3">Each round is equally competitive. The
                            acceptance ratio is the same for all rounds. Most importantly, applicants should dedicate
                            enough time and thought to their application so that it accurately represents their
                            strengths and talents.
                            However, if scholarships are a priority, we encourage applicants to apply in Round 1.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-e-4">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">How should applicants approach the essay
                                section?</p>

                            <img  src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer font-16 font-grey13" id="tab-e-4">The essay section in the application
                            section requires careful consideration and thought. We’re looking for clarity, conciseness,
                            and cohesion in arguments of applicants as well as in the structure of their essay. Most
                            importantly, we encourage them to bring out their most authentic self through these essays
                            to give us the best understanding of their thought process, critical thinking, and
                            communication skills.</p>
                    </div>

                </div>

                <div id="pgp-rise-tab6" class="content">

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-e-5">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">Are the fees refunded in case applicants decide
                                to drop out of the programme?</p>

                            <img  src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer font-16 font-grey13" id="tab-e-5">Fees once submitted are not eligible for
                            refunds.
                            Masters’ Union reserves the right to amend this Refund Policy at any time without prior
                            notice.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-f-1">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">Can applicants defer my admission offer from
                                Masters' Union to the next year?</p>

                            <img  src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer font-16 font-grey13" id="tab-f-1">Currently, we are not offering the option
                            to defer their admission offer. Those who cannot join the programme in the current year are
                            advised to apply again for the next year.
                        </p>
                    </div>


                </div>
